<Base title="Privacy Policy — Fee Simple" description="How Talos handles account information, private workspace content, public records, website analytics and privacy requests." homeOnly>
<Fragment slot="head">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/legal.css">
</Fragment>
  <h1 class="headline">Privacy <span>policy.</span></h1>
  <p class="updated">Effective November 14, 2026</p>

  <main class="doc">
    <p>Talos Operations LLC, a North Carolina company ("Talos", "we" or "us"), operates talosoperations.com and Fee Simple. This policy explains how we handle information on our website, in the Fee Simple app and public demo, and when you contact us. Private customer work and public property records are different categories of information.</p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account and access information.</strong> Your email address, profile information you provide, firm membership and role, invitations, and information needed to authenticate you. If you use Google sign-in, our identity provider receives the profile information supplied for that sign-in. Passwords are handled by our identity provider, not stored as readable passwords in Fee Simple.</li>
      <li><strong>Workspace content.</strong> Matters, client names, file numbers, closing details, saved properties, notes, review status, files and other information you submit or send us. This can include information about your clients and other people.</li>
      <li><strong>Public records and results.</strong> Property identifiers, addresses, owner names, recorded documents, tax and court information, source files, extracted fields, summaries and other results obtained or produced for the Service. Public records can contain personal information even though they are publicly available.</li>
      <li><strong>Communications and business records.</strong> Website access requests, support messages, attachments, correspondence, agreed orders and related billing records. We also keep records needed to administer accounts, agreements and privacy requests.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical information.</strong> IP addresses, browser and device information, page requests, authentication and security events, errors and operational logs. Logs and alerts can contain account emails or property identifiers. This is not a promise that we keep a complete history of everything each user views, downloads or exports.</li>
      <li><strong>Browser storage.</strong> Sign-in cookies and browser storage used for settings, preferences, recent activity and demo or workspace state. Some information stays in your browser rather than being saved to your account.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We receive information from you, authorized people in your firm, public-record sources, identity and infrastructure providers, and your browser when it connects to our services.</p>

    <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide account access, retrieve and organize records, display results, save work and support authorized sharing.</li>
      <li>To administer firms, invitations, agreements and payments, respond to requests and provide support.</li>
      <li>To maintain and secure the Service, investigate errors or misuse, and understand use of the public website.</li>
      <li>To communicate about accounts and services, send product news and promotional offers, and manage communication preferences.</li>
      <li>To comply with law, respond to lawful requests and establish or protect legal rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>We do not sell customer account information or private customer work.</strong> We do not use private workspace content for advertising. Talos's separately contracted lead services do not authorize selling or repurposing your private Fee Simple work.</p>

    <h2>3. Private work and AI tools</h2>
    <p>We do not submit private customer or client information to ChatGPT, Claude, coding agents or other external AI tools, including for support or troubleshooting. We do not use that private information to train general-purpose AI models.</p>
    <p>This commitment concerns private customer and client information. Public source records are handled separately and should not be confused with private notes, client details or files submitted by a customer.</p>

    <h2>4. Firm sharing and Talos access</h2>
    <p>A matter is private to its creator unless it is shared with the firm. Authorized members of the firm can access firm-shared matters and their associated saved work. Individual review notes are separate from notes attached to shared saved work and remain private to their author. People outside the authorized account or firm do not receive access merely by using Fee Simple.</p>
    <p>Sharing settings describe visibility, not legal ownership. Firm work remains subject to the firm's and its clients' rights under our <a href="/terms.html">Terms of Service</a> and applicable agreements. Contact us to arrange access changes or an authorized handover when someone leaves a firm; changing membership is not the same as deleting an account or its content.</p>
    <p>Authorized Talos personnel and service providers can access information as needed to operate, support and secure the Service, carry out authorized requests or meet legal obligations. Administrative access is different from access by another customer. We limit use of private customer work to those purposes.</p>

    <h2>5. Providers and other disclosures</h2>
    <p>We use the following providers for the functions described below. The information each receives depends on the feature you use and whether the connection is made by our server or your browser.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Purpose and information handled</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Google Cloud</td><td>Hosts application infrastructure, databases, public-record files and backups, including account and workspace information.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Provides connection security and access controls; handles network requests and authentication-related information. Its public library service also delivers scripts used by the website.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Auth0 (Okta)</td><td>Handles authentication, account identity, sign-in credentials and verification messages.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Google</td><td>Provides optional Google sign-in, website analytics and web fonts. These features involve identity information or browser requests, depending on the feature.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Microsoft 365</td><td>Handles our email and support correspondence, including messages and attachments you send us.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Netlify</td><td>Hosts the public website and receives website forms, including access requests, plus ordinary hosting logs.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ntfy.sh</td><td>Delivers operational alerts to Talos. Alert content can include sign-in email addresses and property identifiers or error details.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Esri</td><td>Supplies map tiles requested by your browser. Requests disclose network information and the map area being loaded.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><strong>Public-record sources.</strong> Retrieving information can send a property identifier or search details to a county, court or other source. Opening an external source link also connects your browser directly to that source, which handles that visit under its own practices.</p>
    <p>We disclose information to people you authorize, including through firm sharing, and where reasonably necessary to comply with law, respond to lawful process, address fraud or security risks, or protect rights. This does not give us unrestricted permission to disclose private customer work.</p>

    <h2>6. Website analytics, cookies and browser choices</h2>
    <p>The public website uses Google Analytics to measure visits and page use. Analytics cookies and requests can provide Google with browser identifiers, device information, visited pages and interaction information. Analytics currently loads when website pages load; it is not held behind a consent popup.</p>
    <p>Google and other providers contacted by your browser can receive information about visits across sites that use their services, subject to their own practices and your settings. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">Google's explanation of partner-site data</a>. Fonts, scripts and map tiles also create third-party requests, even when they are not used for advertising.</p>
    <p>The authenticated Fee Simple workspace uses cookies and browser storage for sign-in and functionality; it does not include the public website's Google Analytics integration. The public demo can retain demo state in your browser and contact map providers when maps are displayed.</p>
    <p>You can use browser controls to block or clear cookies and local storage. Blocking essential cookies can prevent sign-in, and clearing storage can remove preferences or work saved only on that device. Google also offers a <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a> for supported browsers.</p>
    <p>The website does not currently change its analytics behavior in response to the older Do Not Track browser setting. That setting is distinct from legally recognized privacy preference signals such as Global Privacy Control. Contact us about an applicable privacy choice or signal; we will handle requests and signals as required by applicable law.</p>

    <h2>7. Email communications</h2>
    <p>We use your email address for account and service messages, product news, and promotional offers. You can unsubscribe from promotional emails using the instructions in the email or by contacting <a href="mailto:info@talosoperations.com">info@talosoperations.com</a>. Essential account, security and service messages continue while you use the Service.</p>
    <p>Unsubscribing from marketing does not close your account. We retain the information needed to honor your communication preferences.</p>

    <h2>8. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>Retention depends on the type of information, the service being provided, account and firm instructions, applicable agreements, security needs and legal obligations. Workspace content is retained to provide saved work and is not automatically erased simply because a person stops signing in. Contact us when you want an account closed or information reviewed for deletion.</p>
    <p>Account, support, billing, security and agreement records can be kept where needed to administer the relationship, investigate problems, honor opt-outs, resolve disputes or comply with law. We assess deletion requests against those purposes and any applicable retention requirements. We do not promise one fixed retention period for all records.</p>
    <p>Deleting a matter, removing a saved property, deleting a review note and closing an account are different actions. Deleting a matter can leave saved properties in the account without that matter. Removing a saved property does not necessarily remove a separate review note. Removing someone from a firm does not itself delete that person's account or all associated data.</p>
    <p>Removing a workspace item does not erase the underlying public-record dataset or change a record held by a county, court or other source. Account deletion also does not clear information already stored in your browser or copies you or authorized recipients have downloaded.</p>
    <p>Deleted information can remain in backup copies until those copies are replaced or expire under the applicable backup cycle. Legal obligations or preservation requirements can also require continued retention. We do not promise that deletion immediately removes every backup copy.</p>

    <h2>9. Access, correction and privacy requests</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:info@talosoperations.com">info@talosoperations.com</a> to request access, a copy, correction, deletion or account closure, or to ask about another privacy right. Use your account email where possible and describe the request without sending unnecessary sensitive information.</p>
    <p>We verify identity and authority before acting. For firm or client work, this can include confirming the firm's authority and the rights of other people. A member's account request does not automatically authorize deleting work belonging to a firm or its clients. If you contact us about information we handle for a firm, we may need to coordinate with that firm.</p>
    <p>Available in-app exports may not contain every category of account or workspace information. Contact us for a more complete copy. For an error in a public source record, the source agency may also need to correct its record.</p>
    <p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have additional rights, including access, correction, deletion, portability, objection, restrictions or an appeal of a request decision. We will respond within applicable legal deadlines, explain a denial where required and will not unlawfully discriminate against you for exercising a privacy right.</p>

    <h2>10. Security and processing locations</h2>
    <p>We use encrypted connections, authentication, access controls and database permissions to protect information. No system is perfectly secure. We will provide notices of security incidents as required by applicable law and our agreements.</p>
    <p>Talos operates in the United States and the Service is currently offered for US use. Our primary application hosting is in the United States. Providers can operate infrastructure and support services in other countries, so this policy does not promise that every provider processes all information exclusively in the United States.</p>

    <h2>11. Children</h2>
    <p>Fee Simple accounts are for adults aged 18 or older, and the Service is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided information to us, contact us so we can investigate and address it.</p>

    <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We will post the updated policy and effective date on this page. For material changes, we will provide notice through the app, website or email as appropriate, and obtain consent when required. A policy update does not by itself override commitments made when information was collected.</p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? Email us at <a href="mailto:info@talosoperations.com">info@talosoperations.com</a>.</p>
    <p>Talos Operations LLC · North Carolina, United States</p>
  </main>
</Base>
